  "term": "partial seizure",
  "definition": "A partial seizure is a brief disturbance caused by abnormal electrical activity in one localized area of the brain. It can affect movement, bodily sensations, autonomic functions, or mental experiences such as changes in speech, thought, mood, déjà vu, or hallucination, and it usually happens without a major change in awareness or alertness.",
